"""
Generic 3-DOF (surge/sway/yaw) ship hull dynamics.

The hull is a `PlanarMechanics.Body` with linear body-frame drag (Du, Dv, Dr) plus
optional extra real-input forces and yaw moment. External multibody components
(`Propeller1Q`, `Rudder`, `ShipWind`, `WingSail`, `AntiHeeling`) connect their
`frame_a`s to this hull's `frame_a` to apply their own forces/moments.

Drag and extras are applied through an internal `PlanarMechanics.WorldForceTorque`
configured as `resolve_in_frame = FrameB()`, so all gains and inputs are interpreted
in the body frame.

State equations (from the embedded `Body` block, in world-frame vector form):
```math
m·\\dot v = f + m·g·n
```
```math
I·\\dot w = \\tau
```
where `f`, `\\tau` are summed at `frame_a` from all connected components plus drag and
extra-input contributions.

Outputs `u`, `v`, `r` are the body-frame surge / sway / yaw rate; `pos_x`, `pos_y`,
`psi` are world-frame; `vx_world`, `vy_world` are world-frame velocities.
"""
component Hull3DOF
  parameter mass::Mass = 5e6
  parameter Iz::MomentOfInertia = 5e9
  "Linear surge drag coefficient (≥ 0)"
  parameter Du::Real = 0
  parameter Dv::Real = 0
  parameter Dr::Real = 0

  body = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.Body(m = mass, I = Iz, render = false)
  forcer = MultibodyComponents.PlanarMechanics.WorldForceTorque(
    resolve_in_frame = MultibodyComponents.ResolveInFrame.FrameB()
  )

  "Hull CG / reference frame for connecting accessories"
  frame_a = Frame2D()

  Fx_extra = RealInput()
  Fy_extra = RealInput()
  Mz_extra = RealInput()

  pos_x = RealOutput()
  pos_y = RealOutput()
  psi = RealOutput()
  u = RealOutput()
  v = RealOutput()
  r = RealOutput()
  vx_world = RealOutput()
  vy_world = RealOutput()
relations
  initial body.r = [0, 0]
  initial body.v = [0, 0]
  initial body.phi = 0
  initial body.w = 0

  # World-frame outputs.
  pos_x = body.r[1]
  pos_y = body.r[2]
  psi = body.phi
  vx_world = body.v[1]
  vy_world = body.v[2]
  r = body.w
  # Surge / sway in body frame.
  u = cos(body.phi) * body.v[1] + sin(body.phi) * body.v[2]
  v = -sin(body.phi) * body.v[1] + cos(body.phi) * body.v[2]

  # Drag + extras, in body frame, fed through the WorldForceTorque (resolve in frame_b).
  forcer.force_x = Fx_extra - Du * u
  forcer.force_y = Fy_extra - Dv * v
  forcer.torque = Mz_extra - Dr * r

  # Wire the body, the forcer, and the external frame_a connector together at one node.
  connect(frame_a, body.frame_a, forcer.frame_b)
end
